# GitHub Linguist overrides: the language bar should describe Servette — the
# Python program — not the project website that happens to live beside it.
#
# site/ is the site's own presentation (HTML/JS pages, no build step), marked
# as documentation so Linguist leaves it out of the language statistics.
# The Python that remains counted is the program and its tooling: servette.py,
# src/build.py, src/release.py, tests/test.py. src/*.md was never counted —
# Linguist treats Markdown as prose.
site/** linguist-documentation

# servette.py is generated from src/*.md, but it IS the program — reviewed,
# signed, and shipped as the release artifact — so it must stay counted even
# if a Linguist heuristic ever starts reading its generated-file banner.
servette.py -linguist-generated
